  "proposal": {
    "hypothesis": "Tool selection currently ranks purely by lexical overlap, so an unavailable tool (read_registry_preview, available=0) and a non-read-only mutating tool (update_registry) can outrank the correct read-only live registry tool, and transient errors are never retried because retry is hardcoded to 0. Scoring tools by overlap plus bonuses for availability, read-only safety, entity match, and trusted scope, while making retry a function of retryable (non-permanent) errors, will route to the correct live read-only tool and recover from transient timeouts without granting authority to untrusted or mutating tools.",
