                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "predicted_behavior": "Unavailable and deprecated tools are demoted below the available read-only live registry tool; mutating tools (read_only=0) rank below read-only equivalents with equal overlap. On transient (retryable) tool errors the retry expression evaluates true so the same read-only tool is re-attempted within max_attempts, yielding the live token; permanent errors do not retry. Answers become grounded in the live registry evidence rather than UNKNOWN.",
    "regression_risk": "If a task legitimately requires a mutating tool or an archived/deprecated source, the read-only and non-deprecated bonuses could suppress it; also retrying on any retryable error may consume attempts on tools that repeatedly time out, though max_attempts caps this. Overlap remains the base term so lexical relevance is preserved."
  },
